@startuml 03-class-layers
'============================================================================
'  Sunrise Dental Clinic - CLASS DIAGRAM: the three tiers
'  CIS6003 Advanced Programming (WRIT1), Task A and Task B
'
'  The domain model is on diagram 02 and the design patterns are on diagram
'  04. This one answers a single question: how is the code arranged, and what
'  is allowed to depend on what.
'
'  The one thing to read from it is that every arrow points downwards.
'  Presentation depends on business, business depends on data, and nothing
'  ever points back up. That is what three-tier actually means, and it is why
'  the clinic rules can be tested with no web server and no database at all.
'
'  Only a few methods are shown per class, enough to say what each one is for.
'  Full signatures are on diagram 02 for the domain and diagram 04 for the
'  patterns.
'============================================================================

skinparam shadowing false
skinparam classAttributeIconSize 0
skinparam linetype ortho
skinparam class {
    BackgroundColor #F0FDFA
    BorderColor #0F766E
    HeaderBackgroundColor #CCFBF1
}
skinparam package {
    BackgroundColor #FAFAFA
    BorderColor #9CA3AF
}
skinparam note {
    BackgroundColor #FFFBEB
    BorderColor #B45309
}

title Sunrise Dental Clinic - Three-tier architecture

'============================================================================
package "PRESENTATION TIER" as P <<Rectangle>> {

    package "controller.web  -  the screens staff use" as PW {
        class DashboardWebController <<MVC>>
        class AppointmentWebController <<MVC>>
        class PatientWebController <<MVC>>
        class BillingWebController <<MVC>>
        class ReportWebController <<MVC>>
        class LoginWebController <<MVC>>
        class WebExceptionHandler
    }

    package "controller  -  the web services" as PR {
        class AppointmentRestController
        class PatientRestController
        class BillingRestController
        class ReferenceDataRestController
        class GlobalExceptionHandler
        class CurrentUserResolver
    }
}

'============================================================================
package "BUSINESS LOGIC TIER  (service)" as B <<Rectangle>> {

    class AppointmentService <<Observer subject>> {
        + register(request, createdBy) : Appointment
        + findByNumber(appointmentNo) : Appointment
        + cancel(appointmentNo, reason) : Appointment
        + reschedule(appointmentNo, date, time) : Appointment
        + markCompleted(appointmentNo) : Appointment
    }

    class BillingService {
        + generateBill(appointmentNo, discount, issuedBy) : Bill
        + markPaid(billNo, method) : Bill
        + findUnpaidBills() : List<Bill>
    }

    class PatientService {
        + findOrCreate(request) : Patient
        + findByCode(patientCode) : Patient
        + searchByName(namePart) : List<Patient>
    }

    class ReferenceDataService {
        + bookableDentists() : List<Dentist>
        + bookableTreatments() : List<Treatment>
    }

    class ReportService {
        + revenueByTreatment(from, to) : List<RevenueByTreatmentRow>
        + dentistWorkload(from, to) : List<DentistWorkloadRow>
    }

    class ClinicConfiguration <<Singleton>>
    class BillingStrategyFactory <<Factory>>
    interface AppointmentObserver <<Observer>>
    interface ReferenceNumberGenerator
}

'============================================================================
package "DATA ACCESS TIER  (repository)" as D <<Rectangle>> {
    interface AppointmentRepository <<Repository>>
    interface PatientRepository <<Repository>>
    interface BillRepository <<Repository>>
    interface DentistRepository <<Repository>>
    interface TreatmentRepository <<Repository>>
    interface UserRepository <<Repository>>
    interface ClinicSettingRepository <<Repository>>
}

'============================================================================
package "MySQL 8" as M <<Rectangle>> {
    class "Tables" as Tables <<database>>
    class "Stored procedures\nand functions" as Procs <<database>>
    class "Triggers and\ngenerated columns" as Triggers <<database>>
}

'============================================================================
'  Presentation -> Business
'============================================================================

DashboardWebController --> AppointmentService
DashboardWebController --> BillingService
AppointmentWebController --> AppointmentService
AppointmentWebController --> ReferenceDataService
PatientWebController --> PatientService
BillingWebController --> BillingService
ReportWebController --> ReportService

AppointmentRestController --> AppointmentService
PatientRestController --> PatientService
BillingRestController --> BillingService
ReferenceDataRestController --> ReferenceDataService
CurrentUserResolver --> UserRepository

'============================================================================
'  Business -> Data
'============================================================================

AppointmentService --> AppointmentRepository
AppointmentService --> DentistRepository
AppointmentService --> TreatmentRepository
AppointmentService --> PatientService
AppointmentService --> ClinicConfiguration
AppointmentService --> ReferenceNumberGenerator
AppointmentService --> AppointmentObserver : notifies

BillingService --> BillRepository
BillingService --> AppointmentRepository
BillingService --> BillingStrategyFactory
BillingService --> ReferenceNumberGenerator

PatientService --> PatientRepository
ReferenceDataService --> DentistRepository
ReferenceDataService --> TreatmentRepository
ClinicConfiguration --> ClinicSettingRepository

'============================================================================
'  Data -> MySQL
'============================================================================

AppointmentRepository --> Tables
PatientRepository --> Tables
BillRepository --> Tables
DentistRepository --> Tables
TreatmentRepository --> Tables
UserRepository --> Tables
ClinicSettingRepository --> Tables

ReferenceNumberGenerator --> Procs : CALL
ReportService --> Procs : CALL
Tables ..> Triggers : "writes fire these"

'============================================================================

note right of PR
  Two families of controller, on
  purpose. The screens are how staff
  use the clinic; the web services
  are how another program would,
  which is the "distributed
  application" the brief asks for.

  Both call the same services, so a
  clinic rule cannot be true on one
  and false on the other.
end note

note bottom of B
  Nothing in this tier imports anything
  from the tier above. There is no
  HttpServletRequest, no Model and no
  view name anywhere in it.

  That is what lets 248 tests run with
  no web server and no database.
end note

legend bottom
  |= |= Architectural decision, and why it was made that way |
  | 1 | **The dependency arrows only ever point downwards.** A service never calls a controller. |
  |   | Without that rule the tiers would exist in the folder names only. |
  | 2 | **Two controller families, one business tier.** A rule such as "a visit must be completed |
  |   | before it can be billed" is written once, in BillingService, and both the screen and the |
  |   | web service obey it. |
  | 3 | **The database is a tier, not a store.** Reference numbers come from stored procedures |
  |   | and the reports are stored procedures, because a counter that two receptionists share |
  |   | must be locked by the database, not by Java. |
  | 4 | **The cost.** A one-field change touches four files: entity, repository, service and |
  |   | screen. That is the price of the separation, and it is paid on every small change. |
end legend

@enduml
